# netsurf: plain inline elements inserted between blocks are built alone; :has() rules (never matched here) leave the sibling scan (patch 416)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 415)
#
# The census's top decline after 415, "new element is not a plain block,
# list item or block of blocks" (14). A debug build (scratch only) named
# what each new element held: google 7x a bare <span> inserted among its
# result blocks (between blocks, or after the last), inline SVG (claude,
# bbc, cnnlite), a <video> (youtube), a <table> (wpblog), a custom element
# (google).
#
#  - A plain inline element (an inline tag whose descendants are all
#    plain inline) between blocks takes patch 407's way: built alone, and
#    its run of boxes -- the inline box, its contents, its inline end --
#    moved from the line it was built into to a line of its own after its
#    earlier block (407 moved one box only). One appended after a block
#    takes 378's way: built alone, a line of its own at the end (its own
#    log line; 378's iframe/image line is unchanged).
#  - google's span batches then declined at the sibling check: its sheet
#    is conservative through ".mj3qce:has(.cDeo3)+.CHVz3d". libcss here
#    parses :has() but never matches it (patch 328,
#    selector_never_matches_part) and rejects it inside :not() (fixes360b),
#    so a selector with :has( directly in a compound, or directly inside
#    :not(, never applies: html_rl_prelude_drop_has drops it before the
#    sibling parser reads the prelude (inside a forgiving :is()/:where()
#    only that branch would drop: left alone). rte's ":has(~ ...)" and
#    wpblog's ":not(...:has(...+...))" go too.
#  - The first cut of that scan never stopped on a prelude whose
#    parentheses do not balance (google hung, a 307 s timeout): the
#    prelude's end now always closes the last selector, and the copy is
#    clamped at the end.
#
# google (scratch build): its span batches answered locally (6), no
# sibling declines; rte's insert/remove sibling declines 2 -> 0.
#
